Lets the rust png Bazel build stand on a current Xcode, for mac arm64.

Two changes in toolchain/mac_toolchain_config.bzl:

1. Links with the Xcode ld instead of the downloaded lld. Skia's mac toolchain
   compiles with its own clang 22 and links with its lld against the local
   Xcode SDK. lld 22 cannot read the TAPI stubs of the macOS 27 SDK:

     ld64.lld: error: could not load TAPI file at .../MacSDK/usr/lib/libSystem.tbd: malformed file
     .../libSystem.tbd:4:20: error: unknown architecture
                          arm64e.x1-macos, arm64e.x1-maccatalyst ]

   so the first exec tool (rules_rust's process_wrapper) fails to link.
   Only exec tools are linked here (process_wrapper, build scripts, proc
   macros); the published archives are static libraries and not linked, so
   their contents do not depend on the linker. Without -fuse-ld, clang finds
   ld on PATH (/usr/bin/ld, Xcode's).

2. Lowers the arm64 C++ target from macos12 to macos11, the value GN already
   uses for Skia itself (-target arm64-apple-macos11 in gn/skia/BUILD.gn) and
   rustc's aarch64-apple-darwin default. Otherwise the C++ bridge objects in
   librust_png_ffi_rs.a / libcxx_cc.a say macOS 12 while libskia.a says 11, and
   a consumer that targets 11 gets "built for newer macOS version" warnings.

The x86_64 target is left alone; this repository builds mac arm64 only.

Checked on macOS 27.2 (arm64), Xcode 27.2: bazelisk build @crates//:cxx_cc
//rust/png:ffi_rs --platforms=//bazel/platform:mac_arm64_hermetic.

diff --git a/toolchain/mac_toolchain_config.bzl b/toolchain/mac_toolchain_config.bzl
index 010806d778..4f50485063 100644
--- a/toolchain/mac_toolchain_config.bzl
+++ b/toolchain/mac_toolchain_config.bzl
@@ -351,7 +351,10 @@ def _make_default_flags(ctx, external_toolchain, xcode_macsdk_symlink):
                     # This path is relative to the syslibroot above, and we want lld to look in the
                     # Frameworks symlink that was created in download_mac_toolchain.bzl.
                     "-F/System/Library/Frameworks",
-                    "-fuse-ld=lld",
+                    # skia-prep: link with the Xcode ld (/usr/bin/ld), not the downloaded
+                    # lld. Only exec tools (process_wrapper, build scripts, proc macros) are
+                    # linked here, and lld 22 cannot read the TAPI stubs of newer SDKs
+                    # (macOS 27: "unknown architecture arm64e.x1" in libSystem.tbd).
                     "-std=c++20",
                     # Link against gnu libc that's in the Mac SDK.
                     "-lc++",
@@ -477,7 +480,9 @@ def _make_target_specific_flags(ctx):
         flag_groups = [
             flag_group(
                 flags = [
-                    "--target=arm64-apple-macos12",
+                    # skia-prep: macOS 11, as GN's -target arm64-apple-macos11
+                    # (gn/skia/BUILD.gn) and rustc's aarch64-apple-darwin default.
+                    "--target=arm64-apple-macos11",
                 ],
             ),
         ],
